      "change": "context-behaviour no longer deep-equals the whole context object; it asserts include and exclude separately, treating an absent list and an empty list as the same.",
      "reason": "A drift-brief trial returned { include: [[#main]], exclude: [] } where the reference fix returns { include: [[#main]] }. An empty exclusion list excludes nothing, so both scan exactly the same part of the page. The case exists to catch a scan that silently widens or narrows; the old assertion also failed migrations that are behaviourally identical, which is a validation error, not a product result. Corrected before any comparison was drawn from it, and both conditions are re-run from scratch under the corrected suite rather than re-scored."
